/E ( The foundations of American legislative authority go back to the Declaration of Independence on July 4, 1776. This document marked a significant break from the monarchy and established the idea of popular sovereignty. However, the first attempt at governance under the Articles of Confederation was not effective. This led to the Constitutional Convention of 1787. At this convention, the current U.S. Constitution was created. It shifted from a loose confederacy to a strong federal system. Intense debates took place between Federalists and Anti-Federalists. In the end, they produced a document aimed at forming a more perfect union througha careful balance of shared powers and checks on power. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
