/P 131 0 R
/E (The United States Congress serves as the legislative cornerstone of the federal government, deriving its authority directly from Article I of the Constitution. It is established as a bicameral legislature, divided into the House of Representatives and the Senate, a design intended to balance the immediate passions of the electorate with a more stable, deliberative body. The Senate remains the "Upper House," tasked not only with the creation of law but with )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
