/E (The current as of today, January 24, 2017 \(Start date of Session 1\), political reality was forged on the night of November 8, 2016, in an election decided by fewer than 110,000 votes across three pivotal "Blue Wall" states: Pennsylvania, Michigan, and Wisconsin. Unlike the historical timeline, a surge in urban turnout and a late-stage stabilization of polling in the Rust Belt secured 274 electoral votes for the Clinton-Kaine ticket. However, this victory was not met with national consensus. In the weeks following the election, widespread allegations of "voter irregularities" and a series of unsuccessful but highly publicized legal challenges in the Midwest fueled a "Legitimacy Crisis." )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (As of January 2017, internal polling from the Gallup-Alternative index shows that while 274 electoral votes were certified, 42% of the American public believes the "Blue Wall" states \(WI, MI, PA\) were influenced by foreign cyber-intervention. This has led to the "November 9th Movement," a series of sustained protests in rural counties that have disrupted interstate commerce. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
